hee\-pve\-deploy \-\- deploy and provision a Proxmox LXC from one declarative manifest.

One YAML file per service; this tool creates the container via the real
Proxmox API (pvesh over SSH to the node), idempotent by hostname, then
applies the manifest\[aq]s add\-ons, files and provision scripts inside it.

Real trigger (2026\-08\-24, Spencer): \[dq]build extensible deploy via api to
pve strat\[dq] \-\- tiny, bare\-minimum LXC per core service (bastion, qmail
MTA, snmpd), matching docs/guides/PVE_CAPACITY_PLANNING_METHODOLOGY.md\[aq]s
step 5 (\[dq]a new service is a new manifest entry, not new deploy code\[dq]).

Never installs anything on the pve host itself \-\- pvesh is Proxmox\[aq]s
own real API\-wrapper CLI, already there on any real Proxmox node; this
tool just calls it over SSH from wherever hee runs.

Manifest format (pve/services/<name>.yaml):
  hostname: bastion
  template: alpine\-3.23\-default_20260116_amd64.tar.xz
  cores: 1
  memory_mb: 256
  disk_gb: 4
  storage: ssd1
  bridge: vmbr0
  unprivileged: true
  features: {nesting: true, keyctl: true}   # pve LXC features; only for a container that runs containers
  addons: [agent\-tooling]           # named apk sets from the org\[aq]s registry (\-\-addons)
  agent: ci\-triage                  # agent roster role, only for a container that runs an agent
  files:                            # committed files pushed INTO the container
    \- {src: pve/lab\-dhcp/dnsmasq.conf, dst: /etc/dnsmasq.conf, mode: \[dq]0644\[dq]}
    \- {src: tools/meme\-factory, dst: /opt/meme\-factory}   # a committed DIRECTORY, shipped as one tar
    \- {generate: agent\-roster\-model, dst: /etc/claude\-code/managed\-settings.d/50\-model.json, mode: \[dq]0644\[dq]}
  provision:                        # committed POSIX sh scripts run inside it
    \- pve/lab\-dhcp/provision.sh
  resolver:                         # the container\[aq]s /etc/resolv.conf, and nothing overwrites it
    nameservers: [10.0.0.194, 10.0.0.72]
    search: [lab.tcos.us, tcos.us]
    ndots: 2
  mounts:                           # directories of the pve HOST lent to the container (bind mounts)
    \- {host: /srv/storage, ct: /data/storage}            # read\-write
    \- {host: /srv/media, ct: /data/media, ro: true}      # read\-only

\[ga]files:\[ga] and \[ga]provision:\[ga] paths are relative to the root of the repo the
manifest lives in (git rev\-parse \-\-show\-toplevel), never to the current
directory and never absolute. A \[ga]src\[ga] that is a directory is shipped whole:
every file git tracks under it (\[ga]git ls\-files\[ga], so nothing untracked, no
results/, no .git) goes over as one tar and is unpacked at \[ga]dst\[ga]. Real
trigger (2026\-09\-19): the meme\-factory service is a tree in a PRIVATE repo,
and a container holds no repository credential, so the deploy is the only
honest way the code gets there; the previous shape was a hand \[ga]pct push\[ga] per
file or a clone with a credential the container must not have. \[ga]mode\[ga] is
refused on a directory entry (git\[aq]s own modes travel in the tar): a manifest names what it ships, and what it
ships is under review beside it. Real trigger (2026\-09\-10): the only
precedent for configuring what runs INSIDE a container was a README of
\[ga]pct exec N \-\- sh \-c \[dq]cat > /etc/...\[dq]\[ga] one\-liners (fleet\-ops
pve/snmp\-joe/README.md) \-\- the same imperative shape pve/network.yaml was
written to remove for bridges. Order: create \-> addons \-> files \->
provision. The manifest is fully resolved BEFORE the container is created,
so a missing file fails closed rather than leaving a half\-provisioned
container behind. Every step is previewed under \-\-dry\-run, including
addons, which the dry run used to skip.

A \[ga]files:\[ga] entry names either \[ga]src\[ga] (a committed file) or \[ga]generate\[ga] (a
file rendered at deploy time, never committed). The one generator today is
\[ga]agent\-roster\-model\[ga]: it reads the org\[aq]s agent roster (\-\-agent\-roster), refuses unless
the agent roster is \[ga]status: ratified\[ga] AND its detached signature verifies with a
key the agent roster\[aq]s own ratification_evidence names, then renders the
Claude Code managed\-settings drop\-in that pins the manifest\[aq]s \[ga]agent:\[ga] to
the model the agent roster assigns. Real trigger (2026\-09\-10): the first agent
manifests shipped five hand\-kept managed\-settings.json copies, each
restating a model the signed agent roster already names \-\- a second source that
would leave every container on the old model after an agent roster change, with
nothing to say so. Operator: \[dq]generate from roster at deploy is correct,
footgun\[dq]. The model is named in exactly one place, and the dry run prints
the rendered file.

Every command run inside the container gets
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin. \[ga]pct exec\[ga]
otherwise passes PVE\[aq]s own /sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin, which has no
/usr/local/bin, so a provision script calling a tool it just linked there
exited 127 (measured 2026\-09\-10).

\[ga]resolver:\[ga] declares the container\[aq]s DNS: up to three IPv4 nameservers, in
order; an optional search list; and ndots (default 1). The tool writes
/etc/resolv.conf from it right after the network is up, before add\-ons, and
makes it stick. Nothing else does, measured 2026\-09\-10: the golden template
sets no resolver, pve rewrites /etc/resolv.conf from the HOST\[aq]s file at every
container start, and Alpine\[aq]s udhcpc rewrites it from DHCP on every lease \-\-
ct113 was resolving through 10.0.0.72 and 1.1.1.1 handed out by the
household router, and a public resolver answers NXDOMAIN for lab names. So
it also writes /etc/.pve\-ignore.resolv.conf (pve skips the file), and for a
DHCP container /etc/udhcpc/udhcpc.conf with RESOLV_CONF=\[dq]no\[dq]. ndots matters
on musl: the search list is used only when a name has FEWER dots than
ndots, so \[ga]view.lab\[ga] (one dot) resolves as view.lab.tcos.us only with
ndots 2. Operator: \[dq]proper search and ndot settings too (view.lab/foo should
work)\[dq].

\[ga]mounts:\[ga] lends a directory of the pve HOST to the container, rendered as
\[ga]\-mpN host,mp=ct[,ro=1]\[ga] in manifest order. It is the only way an
unprivileged LXC gets shared storage: the container cannot mount NFS
itself, so the host mounts or serves the storage and bind\-mounts the
directory in. Real trigger (2026\-09\-18): the meme\-factory service needs the
lab\[aq]s $MNTPATH (/data/storage) inside its container, and ipk\-factory has
waited since 2026\-09\-03 for \[dq]the nfs share once set up\[dq] \-\- with no field,
both would have been a hand \[ga]pct set\[ga], the imperative shape this tool exists
to remove. Rules: both paths absolute and normalized (no trailing slash, no
\[ga]..\[ga]), no comma or \[ga]=\[ga] in either (pve\[aq]s option syntax), \[ga]ct\[ga] never \[ga]/\[ga], no
two entries with the same \[ga]ct\[ga]. Known and not hidden: in an unprivileged
container the host\[aq]s uids are shifted (host uid N appears as 100000+N), so
files owned by ordinary host users read as nobody:nogroup \-\- reading needs
the world\-read bit, writing needs a world\-writable (1777) or
100000\-range\-owned directory on the host, and this tool chmods nothing.
pve accepts a bind mount only from root\[at]pam, which pvesh over ssh to root
is. A bind mount is never part of a container backup.

\[ga]\-\-reprovision\[ga] on a hostname that already exists re\-ships every \[ga]files:\[ga]
entry through the identical apply_files() a create uses (directory entries
via the same \[ga]git archive HEAD\[ga] tar) and re\-runs every \[ga]provision:\[ga] script,
in place of the plain idempotent skip. Real trigger,
human\-execution\-engine#760 (2026\-09\-19): the only tool path for the normal
case \-\- a \[ga]provision:\[ga] bug found after the container exists \-\- was \[ga]scp\[ga]
the fix to the node and \[ga]pct exec\[ga] it in by hand, the exact one\-liner shape
this tool exists to retire, on the one flow it had no answer for. It
resolves the manifest fully first, exactly like create, and NEVER runs
\[ga]pct set\[ga]: it cannot touch the container\[aq]s config, so it cannot touch the
MAC a DHCP reservation is keyed on or a mount \-\- those still need a destroy
and a create. Each \[ga]files:\[ga] entry is sha256\-compared against what a
\[ga]pct exec VMID \-\- sha256sum\[ga] finds already in the container (a directory
entry compares every file the tar carries, by path relative to \[ga]dst\[ga]) and
reported \[ga]new\[ga]/\[ga]changed\[ga]/\[ga]unchanged\[ga] before it is re\-shipped, and the
tool\[aq]s own exit code is \[ga]provision:\[ga]\[aq]s own. A live \[ga]mounts:\[ga]/\[ga]features:\[ga]
that no longer matches the manifest (\[ga]pct config VMID\[ga]) is printed as a
\[ga]WARNING\[ga] naming the exact \[ga]pct set\[ga] that would fix it \-\- computed, never
run. On a hostname that does not exist yet, \[ga]\-\-reprovision\[ga] is a no\-op: a
plain create happens, same as without it.
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
hee\-pve\-deploy pve/services/bastion.yaml \-\-dry\-run
    Preview a create: every command, every file, every provision script \-\-
    nothing runs.

hee\-pve\-deploy pve/services/bastion.yaml
    Create it for real. Idempotent by hostname: run again unchanged and it
    only reports the existing container.

hee\-pve\-deploy pve/services/meme\-factory.yaml \-\-reprovision \-\-dry\-run
    Preview a reprovision on an EXISTING container: the sha256 diff of
    every files: entry (new/changed/unchanged), the mounts:/features:
    WARNING if the live config has drifted from the manifest, and the
    provision: scripts that would run. Nothing is applied.

hee\-pve\-deploy pve/services/meme\-factory.yaml \-\-reprovision
    Re\-ship files:, re\-run provision:, on a container that already
    exists. Exit code is provision:\[aq]s own. Never touches mounts:/
    features: \-\- those still need a destroy and a create.
.EE
